        description: "Suggest ROW-LEVEL quality checks based on profiled data. Returns recommendations compatible with create_validation_rule. ONLY suggests row-level checks (NotNull, ValidValues, Format, Length). Does NOT suggest aggregate checks (Uniqueness, Row Counts, Cross-table reconciliation) - For aggregate validation, use: create_duplicate_rule (uniqueness), create_pushdown_rule (row counts, cross-table, referential integrity), create_checksum_rule (count/sum comparison), or create_recon_rule (row-by-row reconciliation). IMPORTANT: All suggested checks for the SAME table should be passed together in a SINGLE call to create_validation_rule. Do NOT split suggestions into separate rules by check type. Combine all checks into one rule to avoid rule sprawl. RETURNS: a 'checksJson' string \u2014 pass it directly to create_validation_rule's checksJson parameter. Do NOT reconstruct the checks array manually.",
